e="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fermented organic acid with its pH regulated so as to range from 6 to 10 by a carbonate, which is applied to cell- or protein-containing material for developing a material which has an appropriate water retentivity, is effective in improving the taste and keeping the freshness, and is free from the fear of adverse effects.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un acide organique fermenté dont le pH est régulé par un carbonate de manière à être compris entre 6 et 10 et que l'on applique à une substance contenant des cellules ou des protéines de manière à produire une substance dotée d'une capacité appropriée de rétention de l'eau. Cet acide peut efficacement améliorer le goût et conserver la fraîcheur et il ne présente aucun effet indésirable.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>